# Ratchet for scripts/check_size_mul_sites.py (make lint-size-mul).
#
# Files that still guard a size product by hand (`SIZE_MAX /`), or check
# that a double fits a size_t against `(double)SIZE_MAX`, instead of calling
# dp_size_mul / dp_size_mul_sat / dp_size_from_double
# (native/inc/doppler/clib_common.h), with how many sites and why. One
# expression is one site: `(double)(SIZE_MAX / 2)` counts once.
#
# THIS LIST MAY ONLY SHRINK. A file not listed may not hold one at all, a
# count left above what its file now has is stale and fails, and nothing
# may be added or raised against the merge base with origin/main.
#
# Format:  <path> <count>  # why
native/src/correlator/correlator_core.c 7  # being rewritten in its own PR (#2958), which moves these onto dp_size_mul / dp_size_from_double and removes this line
